  ],
  "details": "<p><em>The Barrington Atlas Directory</em> notes: Amelia. Given the evidence from Cicero's speech <em>Pro Roscio Amerino</em>, the town was still prosperous ca. 80 BC.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Ameria, claimed by Cato the Elder (quoted by Pliny) as the oldest town in Umbria, was an important center that may have gained Roman municipal status as early as 338 B.C., following the Latin War.",
